WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.480
Two adults stand side by side.

2
00:00:02.530 --> 00:00:03.390
Same height.

3
00:00:03.440 --> 00:00:04.620
Same weight.

4
00:00:04.670 --> 00:00:10.140
So they share the same body mass index,
a number worked out from mass and height.

5
00:00:10.190 --> 00:00:17.510
In one real study across 52 countries,
researchers compared 12 461 people after

6
00:00:17.560 --> 00:00:23.150
a first heart attack with
14 637 who had not had one.

7
00:00:23.200 --> 00:00:27.100
So why might one of them have
a higher risk of heart disease?

8
00:00:27.150 --> 00:00:30.190
In this mission, you'll
calculate body mass index,

9
00:00:30.240 --> 00:00:33.200
and find out what it
can and cannot tell you.

10
00:00:33.250 --> 00:00:38.750
Then you'll read that study's real data,
and test a second quick, cheap measurement.

11
00:00:38.800 --> 00:00:44.040
Your mission: find out why one of two
matching people might face a higher risk.
